{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLRNysLS9smEmxQmovVt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The triage gate now refuses to post \"ready for approval\" when `.ard/<n>/plan.md` is missing. In that case it sets `ard:needs-human` and posts one comment saying the plan file doesn't exist. `go test ./internal/triage/... ./internal/servecmd/...` passes. I did not run the full `make test`.\n\n- **Gate check:** it runs only when the verdict is ready, so the waiting, skipped and other needs-human paths are unchanged. A missing plan also stops the worker from starting when `require_approval` is off.\n- **Errors and recording:** if the check itself fails (for example the fetch of main), the tick returns an error and posts nothing. The next tick retries. A missing plan is recorded as a gate event with reason `no-plan`.\n- **Git fetch:** the check in `internal/servecmd/triage.go` does one git fetch of main per gated issue per tick.\n- **Tests:** the new `TestGateNoPlan` covers the issue's case with approval on and off, a check error, and a role still waiting. Existing gate tests are unchanged because the test fake defaults to \"plan exists\".\n- **Not tested:** I did not add a unit test for the servecmd helper that does the fetch and file read, and I did not change the e2e fixture.\n- **Behaviour change:** a lead-only triage run never writes a `plan.md`, so it now stops at needs-human.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` and `docs/runbooks/gate-2.md` describe the check.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/223/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":762,"cache_read_input_tokens":37765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":762},"output_tokens":522,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_m